    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// Grace notes, and the question the page refuses to answer (docs/plan/prompts/71)." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// A grace note has no written duration. That is not an omission musa has to" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// patch over — it is the fact about grace notes, and the temporal kernel says" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// it exactly: a grace is a *point* occurrence, start equal to end, standing at" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// the onset of the note it leans on." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// So the time it sounds for has to come from somewhere, and *where* is a" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// question Baroque and Romantic practice genuinely disagree about. On the" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// beat, delaying the principal, is an appoggiatura; ahead of it, leaving the" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// principal where the bar puts it, is an acciaccatura. MusicXML settles this" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// in the file — `steal-time-previous=\"50\"` — and so makes the editor decide" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// once, for every performer, forever. musa keeps it where it belongs: two" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// profiles read the same page two ways, and the page is unchanged." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// Compare with `graces-reordered.musa`, which is this piece with one grace" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// group written backwards. The two must not compile to the same kernel term:" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// normalization orders occurrences by span and then by payload, every grace in" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// a group shares a span, so the order is carried in the payload or it is lost." },
